<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Astures</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The peoples of Asturias and León, last in Iberia to fall to Rome in 19 BCE, whose land became the empire's great gold-mining district.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Astures occupied the lands between the Cantabrian coast and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a>, León and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zamora">Zamora</a>, from about the 4th century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> divided them into the Transmontani north of the mountains and the Augustani on the plateau to the south.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived in castros, fortified hilltop villages of round stone houses, in many independent communities grouped by kinship. Herding, farming and metalworking supported them, and their mountains held rich gold deposits. Their main stronghold on the plain was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lancia">Lancia</a>, near León. They spoke a Celtic language.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Astures fought alongside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cantabri">Cantabri</a> in Augustus' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a> of 29 to 19 BCE. After conquest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturica-augusta">Asturica Augusta</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astorga">Astorga</a>) and exploited the gold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/las-medulas">Las Médulas</a> on a vast scale. Their name survives in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturia">Asturias</a> and in the later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-asturias">Kingdom of Asturias</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:7.58%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Asturians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-210&amp;focus=astures" aria-label="Astures on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4595 736 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Astures lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4915 992h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4915 992h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Spain. <a href="/atlas?year=-210&amp;focus=astures">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
